      "text": "Django Architecture and Working",
      "fontSize": 20.94846883733553,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Django Architecture and Working",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ABNAx5sIY_MLndPjtmllW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 410.962990717961,
      "y": 13085.322144579412,
      "width": 737,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1800620573,
      "version": 63,
      "versionNonce": 1062857075,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769931753774,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Django is based on MVT (Model-View-Template) architecture. MVT is a\nsoftware design pattern for developing a web application. It's\nstructure has the following three parts :\n\n1.Model: Acts as the data interface. It defines the structure of\nyour data and is usually backed by a database (e.g., MySQL,\nPostgreSQL).\n\n2.View: A Python function or class that handles web requests. It\ninteracts with the Model and renders a response, typically by\npassing data to a Template.\n\n3.Template: Contains static HTML mixed with Django’s templating\nsyntax. Templates are used to display dynamic data on the web page.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Django is based on MVT (Model-View-Template) architecture. MVT is a software design pattern for developing a web application. It's structure has the following three parts :\n\n1.Model: Acts as the data interface. It defines the structure of your data and is usually backed by a database (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL).\n\n2.View: A Python function or class that handles web requests. It interacts with the Model and renders a response, typically by passing data to a Template.\n\n3.Template: Contains static HTML mixed with Django’s templating syntax. Templates are used to display dynamic data on the web page.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4QSxCrGGfF28dZEEHosYy",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 395.3442797604538,
      "y": 13457.791343881478,
      "width": 822.7745700139034,
      "height": 405.6201735348916,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "transparent",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bq2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 61135443,
      "version": 34,
      "versionNonce": 485004691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769931797542,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "status": "saved",
