      "text": "7.Next, we’ll have to create an application. Django projects are split into one or\nmore applications. Most of our projects will only require one application, but larger\nsites can make use of this ability to split a site into multiple apps. To create an\napplication, we run python manage.py startapp APP_NAME. This will create some\nadditional directories and files that will be useful shortly, including views.py.\n\n8.Now, we have to install our new app. To do this, we go to settings.py, scroll down\nto the list of INSTALLED_APPS, and add the name of our new",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "7.Next, we’ll have to create an application. Django projects are split into one or more applications. Most of our projects will only require one application, but larger sites can make use of this ability to split a site into multiple apps. To create an application, we run python manage.py startapp APP_NAME. This will create some additional directories and files that will be useful shortly, including views.py.\n\n8.Now, we have to install our new app. To do this, we go to settings.py, scroll down to the list of INSTALLED_APPS, and add the name of our new",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
