    {
      "id": "JiFxQwWGPgTvGG6Hk4Rps",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 374.6542795319733,
      "y": 21976.954996622804,
      "width": 1000.7938926324503,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqe",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 953413554,
      "version": 78,
      "versionNonce": 2084210222,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769938342200,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Many sites are parameterized by items included in the URL. For example, going to\nwww.twitter.com/cs50 will show you all of CS50’s tweets, and going to www.github.com/cs50\nwill bring you to CS50’s GitHub page. You can even find your own public GitHub\nrepositories by navigating to www.github.com/YOUR_USERNAME!\n\nIn thinking about how this is implemented, it seems impossible that sites like GitHub and\nTwitter would have an individual URL path for each of its users, so let’s look into how we\ncould make a path that’s a bit more flexible. We’ll start by adding a more general\nfunction, called greet, to views.py:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Many sites are parameterized by items included in the URL. For example, going to www.twitter.com/cs50 will show you all of CS50’s tweets, and going to www.github.com/cs50 will bring you to CS50’s GitHub page. You can even find your own public GitHub repositories by navigating to www.github.com/YOUR_USERNAME!\n\nIn thinking about how this is implemented, it seems impossible that sites like GitHub and Twitter would have an individual URL path for each of its users, so let’s look into how we could make a path that’s a bit more flexible. We’ll start by adding a more general function, called greet, to views.py:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "pAYyjrfIPjjmZqssoYBby",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 381.14649900673726,
      "y": 22239.580395681274,
      "width": 462,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1607399470,
      "version": 58,
      "versionNonce": 720627058,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769938362482,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "def greet(request, name):\n    return HttpResponse(f\"Hello, {name}!\")",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "def greet(request, name):\n    return HttpResponse(f\"Hello, {name}!\")",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FZYV2iAtR5hzCJR4ORYBe",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 376.2139259590406,
      "y": 22236.126267243842,
      "width": 495.57693034614636,
      "height": 63.42912259561854,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqi",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 139112690,
      "version": 55,
      "versionNonce": 1967623150,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769938371132,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G2b2qqH9nW3YTEdgI-RiX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 372.2829808038998,
      "y": 22338.372061882605,
      "width": 737,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bqj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1498914162,
      "version": 49,
      "versionNonce": 1773295278,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769938387398,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This function takes in not only a request, but also an additional\nargument of a user’s name, and then returns a custom HTTP Response\nbased on that name. Next, we have to create a more flexible path in\nurls.py, which could look something like this:\n\npath(\"<str:name>\", views.greet, name=\"greet\")",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This function takes in not only a request, but also an additional argument of a user’s name, and then returns a custom HTTP Response based on that name. Next, we have to create a more flexible path in urls.py, which could look something like this:\n\npath(\"<str:name>\", views.greet, name=\"greet\")",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
